   },
   "source": [
    "\n",
    " \"cells\": [\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Artifact rejection in EEG signals\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Electroencephalographic (EEG) recordings are routinely contaminated by\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**artifacts** — signals of non-cerebral origin that overlap, both in time\\n\",\n",
    "    \"and frequency, with the brain activity of interest. Ocular artifacts\\n\",\n",
    "    \"produced by eye blinks and saccades (recorded by the **electrooculogram**,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"EOG) are among the most pervasive: they have large amplitudes and project\\n\",\n",
    "    \"strongly onto frontal electrodes, easily masking the underlying EEG.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"`medusa-kernel` ships everything needed to study and mitigate these\\n\",\n",
    "    \"artifacts without any acquisition hardware. In this tutorial we will:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Synthesise** a realistic multi-channel EEG using\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  `medusa.signal.generators`, and contaminate it with a biologically\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  plausible EOG (blinks, saccades and slow drift).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Reject the artifacts with the three complementary methods available in\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  `medusa.signal.artifact_removal`:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    1. **Regression** against a reference EOG channel\\n\",\n",
    "    \"       (`ArtifactRegression`).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    2. **Independent Component Analysis** (`ICA`) for blind source\\n\",\n",
    "    \"       separation.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    3. **Amplitude-threshold epoch rejection** (`reject_noisy_epochs`).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Visualise the results with the MEDUSA plotting style, including\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  topographic head maps.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Because the data are synthetic we know the **ground-truth** clean EEG, so\\n\",\n",
    "    \"we can quantify how well each method recovers it.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"📘 *For reference, see the [Medusa documentation](https://docs.medusabci.com).*\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Imports\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Install dependencies if you are running this notebook on Google Colab.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"<div class=\\\"alert alert-block alert-danger\\\">\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Important: execute the following cell <b>only</b> if you are using Google Colab!\\n\",\n",
    "    \"</div>\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"b90805cfc25b91ca\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:49:59.634014700Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:49:59.336392100Z\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"source\": \"!pip install medusa-kernel\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"995a24b89d70b2de\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"name\": \"stderr\",\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"stream\",\n",
    "     \"text\": [\n",
    "      \"\\\"pip\\\" no se reconoce como un comando interno o externo,\\n\",\n",
    "      \"programa o archivo por lotes ejecutable.\\n\",\n",
    "      \"\\\"pip\\\" no se reconoce como un comando interno o externo,\\n\",\n",
    "      \"programa o archivo por lotes ejecutable.\\n\"\n",
    "     ]\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 14\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"source\": \"Import the modules that will be used in this notebook.\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"484198a417a3f9c6\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:50:24.399216900Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:50:24.371578600Z\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# General imports\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import numpy as np\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.style.use('seaborn-v0_8')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Medusa imports\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from medusa.signal.generators import EEGSignalGenerator, EOGSignalGenerator\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from medusa.signal.artifact_removal import (\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ArtifactRegression, ICA, reject_noisy_epochs)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from medusa.signal.frequency_filtering import IIRFilter\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from medusa.signal.segmentation import segment_signal\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from medusa.core.data.biosignals.eeg.eeg import EEGChannelSet\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from medusa.plots.head_plots import TopographicPlot\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# MEDUSA-style color palette used throughout the notebook\\n\",\n",
    "    \"C_CLEAN = '#219C90'   # teal  -> ground-truth EEG\\n\",\n",
    "    \"C_DIRTY = '#D83F31'   # red   -> contaminated EEG\\n\",\n",
    "    \"C_REC = '#EE9322'     # amber -> recovered EEG\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('\\\\n> All required packages were successfully imported')\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"9532b7d7f058170c\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"name\": \"stdout\",\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"stream\",\n",
    "     \"text\": [\n",
    "      \"\\n\",\n",
    "      \"> All required packages were successfully imported\\n\"\n",
    "     ]\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 18\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Generate a contaminated EEG recording\\n\",\n",
    "    \"We first synthesise a clean, multi-channel EEG with\\n\",\n",
    "    \"`EEGSignalGenerator`, which models the signal as a `1/f` background plus\\n\",\n",
    "    \"narrow-band oscillatory rhythms (e.g., the occipital alpha rhythm). Each\\n\",\n",
    "    \"channel is generated independently and amplitudes are expressed in\\n\",\n",
    "    \"microvolts.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Next, we synthesise an ocular source with `EOGSignalGenerator`, which\\n\",\n",
    "    \"combines **eye blinks** (large Gaussian deflections), **saccades** (smooth\\n\",\n",
    "    \"baseline steps) and **slow drift**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Finally, we **mix** the EOG into the EEG. Ocular activity spreads across\\n\",\n",
    "    \"the scalp by volume conduction, so its contribution is strongest at the\\n\",\n",
    "    \"frontal electrodes (Fp1, Fp2, F7, F8) and progressively weaker towards the\\n\",\n",
    "    \"occipital ones. We model this with a per-channel weight vector — the\\n\",\n",
    "    \"*contamination topography*.\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"3f2f0f502abd65fd\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:50:31.748103100Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:50:31.720595800Z\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Acquisition parameters\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fs = 250.0          # Sampling rate (Hz)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"duration = 20.0     # Recording length (s)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# 10-20 montage (frontal channels first, occipital last)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"channels = ['Fp1', 'Fp2', 'F7', 'F3', 'Fz', 'F4', 'F8',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            'C3', 'Cz', 'C4', 'P3', 'Pz', 'P4', 'O1', 'Oz', 'O2']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"n_channels = len(channels)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# --- Ground-truth EEG ---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"eeg_gen = EEGSignalGenerator(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    fs=fs,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    oscillations=[(10.0, 15.0), (6.0, 8.0)],  # alpha + theta rhythms\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    background_amplitude=15.0,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    seed=42)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"clean_eeg = eeg_gen.get_chunk(duration, n_channels)  # (n_samples, n_channels)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# --- Ocular source (single EOG reference channel) ---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"eog_gen = EOGSignalGenerator(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    fs=fs, blink_rate=18.0, blink_amplitude=180.0,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    saccade_rate=20.0, saccade_amplitude=40.0, drift_amplitude=8.0,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    seed=7)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"eog = eog_gen.get_chunk(duration, 1)  # (n_samples, 1)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# --- Contamination topography (frontal > occipital) ---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"weights_map = {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    'Fp1': 1.00, 'Fp2': 1.00, 'F7': 0.80, 'F8': 0.80,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    'F3': 0.60, 'Fz': 0.55, 'F4': 0.60,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    'C3': 0.30, 'Cz': 0.25, 'C4': 0.30,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    'P3': 0.12, 'Pz': 0.10, 'P4': 0.12,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    'O1': 0.05, 'Oz': 0.05, 'O2': 0.05,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"weights = np.array([weights_map[ch] for ch in channels])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Mix: broadcast the EOG onto every channel scaled by its weight\\n\",\n",
    "    \"contaminated_eeg = clean_eeg + eog * weights[None, :]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Time vector\\n\",\n",
    "    \"times = np.arange(clean_eeg.shape[0]) / fs\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('> Synthetic recording ready')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'   - Signal shape (samples, channels): {contaminated_eeg.shape}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'   - Sampling rate (Hz): {fs}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'   - Channels: {channels}')\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"c72d1f634a331a8f\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"name\": \"stdout\",\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"stream\",\n",
    "     \"text\": [\n",
    "      \"> Synthetic recording ready\\n\",\n",
    "      \"   - Signal shape (samples, channels): (5000, 16)\\n\",\n",
    "      \"   - Sampling rate (Hz): 250.0\\n\",\n",
    "      \"   - Channels: ['Fp1', 'Fp2', 'F7', 'F3', 'Fz', 'F4', 'F8', 'C3', 'Cz', 'C4', 'P3', 'Pz', 'P4', 'O1', 'Oz', 'O2']\\n\"\n",
    "     ]\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 19\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Visualise the contamination\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Let's compare the clean and contaminated signals on a frontal channel\\n\",\n",
    "    \"(Fp1, heavily affected) and an occipital one (Oz, barely affected). The\\n\",\n",
    "    \"large transient deflections in Fp1 are the eye blinks. We also display the\\n\",\n",
    "    \"*contamination topography* using a MEDUSA `TopographicPlot`.\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"af33e2cecbfb8e4d\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:50:50.074842Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:50:49.489783500Z\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"fig = plt.figure(figsize=(12, 4))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"gs = fig.add_gridspec(2, 3, width_ratios=[2, 2, 1.2])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Frontal channel Fp1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax1 = fig.add_subplot(gs[0, 0:2])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"idx_fp1 = channels.index('Fp1')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax1.plot(times, contaminated_eeg[:, idx_fp1], color=C_DIRTY,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"         label='Contaminated', linewidth=0.8)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax1.plot(times, clean_eeg[:, idx_fp1], color=C_CLEAN,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"         label='Ground-truth', linewidth=0.8)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax1.set_title('Frontal channel (Fp1)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax1.set_ylabel('Amplitude (uV)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax1.legend(loc='upper right')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax1.set_xlim(0, duration)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Occipital channel Oz\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax2 = fig.add_subplot(gs[1, 0:2])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"idx_oz = channels.index('Oz')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax2.plot(times, contaminated_eeg[:, idx_oz], color=C_DIRTY,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"         label='Contaminated', linewidth=0.8)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax2.plot(times, clean_eeg[:, idx_oz], color=C_CLEAN,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"         label='Ground-truth', linewidth=0.8)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax2.set_title('Occipital channel (Oz)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax2.set_xlabel('Time (s)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax2.set_ylabel('Amplitude (uV)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax2.set_xlim(0, duration)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Contamination topography\\n\",\n",
    "    \"channel_set = EEGChannelSet()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"channel_set.set_standard_montage(channels)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax3 = fig.add_subplot(gs[:, 2])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"topo = TopographicPlot(axes=ax3, channel_set=channel_set,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                       cmap='YlOrRd', plot_channel_labels=True,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                       head_line_width=1.5)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"topo.update(values=weights)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax3.set_title('EOG contamination\\\\ntopography')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"cbar = fig.colorbar(topo.plot_handles['color-mesh'], ax=ax3,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                    fraction=0.046, pad=0.04)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"cbar.set_label('Mixing weight')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"18726485a932e3f7\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"data\": {\n",
    "      \"text/plain\": [\n",
    "       \"<Figure size 1200x400 with 4 Axes>\"\n",
    "      ],\n",
    "      \"image/png\": \"\"\n",
    "     },\n",
    "     \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"display_data\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 20\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Method 1 — Artifact regression\\n\",\n",
    "    \"When the artifact is **recorded simultaneously** with a reference sensor\\n\",\n",
    "    \"(here, the EOG channel), the simplest and most robust correction is\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**linear regression**: for every EEG channel we estimate, by least squares,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"how much of the reference signal leaks into it, and subtract that\\n\",\n",
    "    \"contribution.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The `ArtifactRegression` class follows the scikit-learn `fit` / `transform`\\n\",\n",
    "    \"convention. As recommended in its documentation, both the EEG and the\\n\",\n",
    "    \"reference EOG should be band-pass filtered beforehand; we apply a 1–40 Hz\\n\",\n",
    "    \"IIR filter.\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"45d38e853d89f055\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:51:44.814242900Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:51:44.754606Z\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Band-pass filter (1-40 Hz) both the EEG and the EOG reference\\n\",\n",
    "    \"iir = IIRFilter(order=4, cutoff=(1.0, 40.0), btype='bandpass',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                filt_method='sosfiltfilt')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"eeg_filt = iir.fit_transform(contaminated_eeg, fs)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"iir_eog = IIRFilter(order=4, cutoff=(1.0, 40.0), btype='bandpass',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                    filt_method='sosfiltfilt')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"eog_filt = iir_eog.fit_transform(eog, fs)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Regress the EOG reference out of the EEG\\n\",\n",
    "    \"reg = ArtifactRegression()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"clean_reg = reg.fit_transform(eeg_filt, eog_filt)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('> Artifact regression applied')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'   - Cleaned signal shape: {clean_reg.shape}')\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"22c4849412b1477f\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"name\": \"stdout\",\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"stream\",\n",
    "     \"text\": [\n",
    "      \"> Artifact regression applied\\n\",\n",
    "      \"   - Cleaned signal shape: (5000, 16)\\n\"\n",
    "     ]\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 21\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:51:49.687370500Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:51:49.536829500Z\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Compare on the frontal channel Fp1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 3))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.plot(times, eeg_filt[:, idx_fp1], color=C_DIRTY,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        label='Contaminated', linewidth=0.8, alpha=0.7)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.plot(times, clean_reg[:, idx_fp1], color=C_REC,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        label='Regression', linewidth=0.9)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_title('Artifact regression — frontal channel (Fp1)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_xlabel('Time (s)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_ylabel('Amplitude (uV)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_xlim(0, duration)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.legend(loc='upper right')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"7b965d83a2ca242d\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"data\": {\n",
    "      \"text/plain\": [\n",
    "       \"<Figure size 1200x300 with 1 Axes>\"\n",
    "      ],\n",
    "      \"image/png\": \"\"\n",
    "     },\n",
    "     \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"display_data\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 22\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"The blink and saccade deflections have been almost entirely removed while\\n\",\n",
    "    \"the underlying EEG rhythms are preserved.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Method 2 — Independent Component Analysis (ICA)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Regression requires a clean reference channel. When none is available, we\\n\",\n",
    "    \"can resort to **blind source separation**. ICA decomposes the multi-channel\\n\",\n",
    "    \"EEG into a set of maximally independent components; artifactual sources\\n\",\n",
    "    \"(such as ocular activity) typically concentrate into one or a few\\n\",\n",
    "    \"components that can be identified and removed before reconstructing the\\n\",\n",
    "    \"signal.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"We fit the `ICA` model and inspect the spatial topographies of the\\n\",\n",
    "    \"components.\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"b15567a41fc81858\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:52:03.252699700Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:52:00.072892200Z\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Fit ICA on the (filtered) contaminated EEG\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ica = ICA(random_state=0)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ica.fit(eeg_filt, l_cha=channels, fs=fs, n_components=n_channels)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Plot the spatial topographies of every component\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig_comp = ica.plot_components(cmap='bwr')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig_comp.set_size_inches(12, 6)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.suptitle('ICA components (spatial topographies)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"10e3ee253c4229cd\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"name\": \"stderr\",\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"stream\",\n",
    "     \"text\": [\n",
    "      \"D:\\\\Eduardo\\\\Proyectos\\\\medusa\\\\medusa-kernel\\\\src\\\\medusa\\\\signal\\\\artifact_removal.py:470: UserWarning: FigureCanvasAgg is non-interactive, and thus cannot be shown\\n\",\n",
    "      \"  fig.show()\\n\"\n",
    "     ]\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"data\": {\n",
    "      \"text/plain\": [\n",
    "       \"<Figure size 1200x600 with 20 Axes>\"\n",
    "      ],\n",
    "      \"image/png\": \"\"\n",
    "     },\n",
    "     \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"display_data\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 23\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Identify the ocular component\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Since we have the ground-truth EOG, we can identify the artifactual\\n\",\n",
    "    \"component **objectively** as the one whose source activation correlates the\\n\",\n",
    "    \"most with the EOG reference. In a real scenario this step is usually done\\n\",\n",
    "    \"by visual inspection of the frontal topography and the blink-like time\\n\",\n",
    "    \"course of each component.\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"fa648161f6f28086\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:49:58.063353700Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:49:57.609916Z\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Source activations: (n_samples, n_components)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sources = ica.get_sources(eeg_filt)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Correlate each source with the EOG reference\\n\",\n",
    "    \"corrs = np.array([\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    abs(np.corrcoef(sources[:, i], eog_filt[:, 0])[0, 1])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for i in range(sources.shape[1])])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"art_idx = int(np.argmax(corrs))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'> Most ocular-like component: ICA_{art_idx} '\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      f'(|r| = {corrs[art_idx]:.2f} with the EOG)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Inspect the artifact component: spatial topography + source time course\\n\",\n",
    "    \"components = ica.get_components()  # (n_channels, n_components)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig = plt.figure(figsize=(12, 3.5))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"gs = fig.add_gridspec(1, 2, width_ratios=[1, 2.5])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Frontal topography of the ocular component\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax_topo = fig.add_subplot(gs[0, 0])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"topo = TopographicPlot(axes=ax_topo, channel_set=channel_set, cmap='bwr',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                       head_line_width=1.5)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"topo.update(values=components[:, art_idx])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax_topo.set_title(f'ICA_{art_idx} topography')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Source time course (blink-like deflections)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax_src = fig.add_subplot(gs[0, 1])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax_src.plot(times, sources[:, art_idx], color=C_DIRTY, linewidth=0.8)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax_src.set_title(f'ICA_{art_idx} source activation')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax_src.set_xlabel('Time (s)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax_src.set_ylabel('Amplitude (n.u.)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax_src.set_xlim(0, duration)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"be4a0cf71172140d\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"name\": \"stdout\",\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"stream\",\n",
    "     \"text\": [\n",
    "      \"> Most ocular-like component: ICA_0 (|r| = 0.96 with the EOG)\\n\"\n",
    "     ]\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"data\": {\n",
    "      \"text/plain\": [\n",
    "       \"<Figure size 1200x350 with 2 Axes>\"\n",
    "      ],\n",
    "      \"image/png\": \"\"\n",
    "     },\n",
    "     \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"display_data\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 8\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:52:52.327841300Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:52:52.179494700Z\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Rebuild the EEG excluding the ocular component\\n\",\n",
    "    \"clean_ica = ica.rebuild(eeg_filt, exclude=[art_idx])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Compare on the frontal channel Fp1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 3))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.plot(times, eeg_filt[:, idx_fp1], color=C_DIRTY,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        label='Contaminated', linewidth=0.8, alpha=0.7)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.plot(times, clean_ica[:, idx_fp1], color=C_REC,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        label='ICA-cleaned', linewidth=0.9)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_title('ICA artifact rejection — frontal channel (Fp1)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_xlabel('Time (s)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_ylabel('Amplitude (uV)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_xlim(0, duration)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.legend(loc='upper right')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"3e8a1c93b52adfae\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"data\": {\n",
    "      \"text/plain\": [\n",
    "       \"<Figure size 1200x300 with 1 Axes>\"\n",
    "      ],\n",
    "      \"image/png\": \"\"\n",
    "     },\n",
    "     \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"display_data\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 24\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Method 3 — Amplitude-threshold epoch rejection\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The previous two methods *correct* the signal. A complementary, more\\n\",\n",
    "    \"conservative strategy is to **reject** the segments that are too\\n\",\n",
    "    \"contaminated to be trusted — useful, for instance, before averaging epochs\\n\",\n",
    "    \"in an ERP analysis.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"`reject_noisy_epochs` discards any epoch containing at least `n_samp`\\n\",\n",
    "    \"samples that exceed `k` standard deviations from the channel mean, in at\\n\",\n",
    "    \"least `n_cha` channels. We first split the recording into 2-second\\n\",\n",
    "    \"non-overlapping segments with `segment_signal`.\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"c963ccf190c59b8a\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:53:53.433378700Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:53:53.408479900Z\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Split into 2-second non-overlapping epochs\\n\",\n",
    "    \"segment_length = int(2.0 * fs)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"epochs = segment_signal(contaminated_eeg, segment_length=segment_length)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Per-channel statistics over the whole recording\\n\",\n",
    "    \"signal_mean = contaminated_eeg.mean(axis=0)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"signal_std = contaminated_eeg.std(axis=0)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Reject noisy epochs\\n\",\n",
    "    \"pct_rejected, clean_epochs, rejected_idx = reject_noisy_epochs(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    epochs, signal_mean, signal_std, k=3, n_samp=2, n_cha=1)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'> Epoch rejection summary')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'   - Total epochs:    {epochs.shape[0]}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'   - Rejected epochs: {int(rejected_idx.sum())} '\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      f'({pct_rejected:.1f}%)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'   - Kept epochs:     {clean_epochs.shape[0]}')\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"3e055ab225b75971\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"name\": \"stdout\",\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"stream\",\n",
    "     \"text\": [\n",
    "      \"> Epoch rejection summary\\n\",\n",
    "      \"   - Total epochs:    10\\n\",\n",
    "      \"   - Rejected epochs: 7 (70.0%)\\n\",\n",
    "      \"   - Kept epochs:     3\\n\"\n",
    "     ]\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 25\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:53:56.420202900Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:53:56.257847800Z\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Visualise which epochs were rejected on the Fp1 channel\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 3))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.plot(times, contaminated_eeg[:, idx_fp1], color=C_DIRTY,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        linewidth=0.8, label='Contaminated')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for e in range(epochs.shape[0]):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    t0 = e * segment_length / fs\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    t1 = (e + 1) * segment_length / fs\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if rejected_idx[e]:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ax.axvspan(t0, t1, color=C_DIRTY, alpha=0.15)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ax.axvspan(t0, t1, color=C_CLEAN, alpha=0.10)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_title('Epoch rejection — frontal channel (Fp1)  '\\n\",\n",
    "    \"             '(red = rejected, green = kept)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_xlabel('Time (s)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_ylabel('Amplitude (uV)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.set_xlim(0, duration)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax.legend(loc='upper right')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"b550bc1eb5217de2\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"data\": {\n",
    "      \"text/plain\": [\n",
    "       \"<Figure size 1200x300 with 1 Axes>\"\n",
    "      ],\n",
    "      \"image/png\": \"\"\n",
    "     },\n",
    "     \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"display_data\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 26\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Quantitative comparison\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Because the ground-truth clean EEG is known, we can measure how well each\\n\",\n",
    "    \"*correction* method recovers it. We use the residual root-mean-square\\n\",\n",
    "    \"error (RMSE) against the ground truth, **averaged across channels**, and\\n\",\n",
    "    \"summarise it with a topographic map of the residual error before and after\\n\",\n",
    "    \"cleaning.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Note: to compare fairly, we use the band-pass filtered ground truth as the\\n\",\n",
    "    \"reference for the regression / ICA outputs (both operate on the filtered\\n\",\n",
    "    \"signal).\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"1570bb9aa8e43e1\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:54:06.131478Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:54:06.106874600Z\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Filtered ground truth (same preprocessing as the corrected signals)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"clean_eeg_filt = IIRFilter(order=4, cutoff=(1.0, 40.0), btype='bandpass',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                           filt_method='sosfiltfilt').fit_transform(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    clean_eeg, fs)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def rmse_per_channel(estimate, reference):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return np.sqrt(np.mean((estimate - reference) ** 2, axis=0))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"rmse_dirty = rmse_per_channel(eeg_filt, clean_eeg_filt)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"rmse_reg = rmse_per_channel(clean_reg, clean_eeg_filt)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"rmse_ica = rmse_per_channel(clean_ica, clean_eeg_filt)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('> Mean residual RMSE vs. ground truth (uV)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'   - Contaminated: {rmse_dirty.mean():.2f}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'   - Regression:   {rmse_reg.mean():.2f}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'   - ICA:          {rmse_ica.mean():.2f}')\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"d3eb2cee37b57c95\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"name\": \"stdout\",\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"stream\",\n",
    "     \"text\": [\n",
    "      \"> Mean residual RMSE vs. ground truth (uV)\\n\",\n",
    "      \"   - Contaminated: 8.98\\n\",\n",
    "      \"   - Regression:   0.42\\n\",\n",
    "      \"   - ICA:          2.61\\n\"\n",
    "     ]\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 27\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:54:38.436302900Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-06-04T17:54:37.384171400Z\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Bar chart of mean RMSE + residual-error topographies\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig = plt.figure(figsize=(12, 4))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"gs = fig.add_gridspec(1, 4, width_ratios=[1.3, 1, 1, 1])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Bar chart\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax_bar = fig.add_subplot(gs[0, 0])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"labels = ['Contaminated', 'Regression', 'ICA']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"values = [rmse_dirty.mean(), rmse_reg.mean(), rmse_ica.mean()]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax_bar.bar(labels, values, color=[C_DIRTY, C_REC, C_CLEAN])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax_bar.set_ylabel('Mean residual RMSE (uV)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax_bar.set_title('Recovery error')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ax_bar.tick_params(axis='x', rotation=20)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Common color limits for the topographies\\n\",\n",
    "    \"clim = (0, float(rmse_dirty.max()))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"topo_data = [('Contaminated', rmse_dirty),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"             ('Regression', rmse_reg),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"             ('ICA', rmse_ica)]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for i, (title, values) in enumerate(topo_data):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax = fig.add_subplot(gs[0, i + 1])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    topo = TopographicPlot(axes=ax, channel_set=channel_set,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                           cmap='YlOrRd', clim=clim, head_line_width=1.5)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    topo.update(values=values)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.set_title(f'{title}\\\\nresidual')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    cbar = fig.colorbar(topo.plot_handles['color-mesh'], ax=ax,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                        fraction=0.046, pad=0.04)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    cbar.set_label('RMSE (uV)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"87e4f963581e2e53\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"data\": {\n",
    "      \"text/plain\": [\n",
    "       \"<Figure size 1200x400 with 7 Axes>\"\n",
    "      ],\n",
    "      \"image/png\": \"\"\n",
    "     },\n",
    "     \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"display_data\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 28\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"The residual-error topographies make the spatial nature of the ocular\\n\",\n",
    "    \"artifact evident: before cleaning, the error is concentrated over the\\n\",\n",
    "    \"frontal electrodes, exactly where the EOG projects most strongly. Both the\\n\",\n",
    "    \"regression and ICA approaches drastically reduce the frontal error,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"recovering an EEG much closer to the ground truth.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Summary and next steps\\n\",\n",
    "    \"In this tutorial we have:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Generated a realistic EEG contaminated with EOG artifacts using the\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  synthetic generators in `medusa.signal.generators`.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Removed the artifacts with the three methods of\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  `medusa.signal.artifact_removal`:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    - **`ArtifactRegression`** — fast and accurate when a reference EOG\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      channel is available.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    - **`ICA`** — blind source separation that needs no reference, at the\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      cost of identifying the artifactual component(s).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    - **`reject_noisy_epochs`** — conservative amplitude-threshold rejection\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      of unusable segments.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Validated and compared the results against the known ground truth using\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  MEDUSA topographic plots.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### What's next?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Combine **epoch rejection** with **regression / ICA** in a full\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  preprocessing pipeline.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Experiment with the generator parameters (blink rate, amplitude, drift)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  and the rejection thresholds (`k`, `n_samp`, `n_cha`).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Apply these methods to real recordings loaded with\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  `medusa.core.data.recording.Recording`.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"See you in the next MEDUSA tutorial!\\n\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"b7fc970debdcc8cf\"\n",
    "  }\n",
    " ],\n",
    " \"metadata\": {},\n",
    " \"nbformat\": 4,\n",
    " \"nbformat_minor\": 5\n",
    "}"
   ],
